- Summary:: Sam Green's film "32 Sounds" explores the significance of sound in our lives, using various recordings to reflect on themes like memory and connection. Inspired by composer Annea Lockwood, who has recorded river sounds for over 50 years, Green highlights her unique contributions to music and the importance of "listening with" our environment. As interest in Lockwood grows, she is finally receiving recognition for her long-standing, impactful work in the avant-garde music scene.
